-- Kentucky WARN history, 2020 onward. Additive and safe to re-run.
--
-- Why: the weekly importer (src/lib/warn/sync.ts) skips any notice older than MAX_AGE_DAYS (540 days), so Kentucky's "Prior Year Warn Notices"
-- workbook (sheets 2017-2025, https://kyworks.ky.gov/Services/Documents/Prior%20Year%20Warn%20Notices.xlsx) was fetched every week and almost all of
-- it thrown away: the database held only notices from May 2025 on. This inserts the 357 distinct notices received 2020-01-01 or later
-- from that workbook and the 2026-11-04 current report. source stays WARN_FILING; companyId is left null (UNMATCHED) so no Company rows are created.
--
-- A notice is the same one when employer, notice date and headcount agree: the table is unique on (state, normalizedEmployer, noticeDate,
-- employees). Where two counties share that key (GDI 2024-01-04 / 40 in Taylor and Fayette; P.F. Chang's 2020-09-18 / 75 in Jefferson and
-- Fayette) one row is kept, the Jefferson one if there is one. County is stored bare ("Jefferson"). A second run inserts nothing.
--
-- Also sets the county text on existing Kentucky Jefferson rows to "Jefferson" (8 rows were "Jefferson County - Louisville", dated
-- 2026-01-31 to 2026-10-12). Display text only: countyKey() in src/lib/workforce/places.ts reads both spellings the same way.
-- In the VALUES list the source file is a code: P = Prior Year Warn Notices.xlsx, C = Website-WARN Notice Report 11042026.xlsx.
WITH v(employer,"normalizedEmployer","noticeDate","effectiveDate",employees,"layoffType",county,industry,"sourceUrl") AS (
